  "verification_note": "Fix round 3 (2026-11-13): resolved the supervisor's full-Python failure, a 30-second timeout in test_cli_rejects_planted_violations_without_executing_them. The cause predated this node's pattern changes: every check in all_static() re-read and re-parsed the same sources (160 ast.parse calls over 24 files, up to 7 per file, reproduced at the base commit in static-before-round3.log), and on the shared 8-core machine at load average ~45 one CLI subprocess exceeded the test's 30s limit. One all_static() run now reads and parses each source once (24 parses) and shares the results between checks; the cache is active only inside the run and released afterwards, direct check calls always read fresh, and verdicts are unchanged (static 13/13). Three new regressions pin parse-once-per-run, identical results with cache release, and fresh reads on direct calls. Final results: Python 1607 tests (1604 + 3 new), 6 existing skips, no failures, 490.097s, exit 0; runner 61 passed in 544.580s; dry-run 695 checks / 33 required IDs; static 13/13; spec 46/46 and 72/72; tracked-secrets passed; focused secret scan 27 and static 22 passed. Daemon report headers were rewritten with the current source tree hash and reports/unittest.log now excerpts all four daemon modules (356 tests: 300 dry-run, 27 secret scan, 22 static, 7 required coverage) from python-round3.log. Rust/codegen sources are unchanged this round, so round-2 Rust evidence (514 passed/1 ignored, codegen 130, fmt/clippy) remains valid; vocabulary/validation/blueprint checks keep their round-2 logs as their inputs did not change. The design bundle's spec-check log body matches the current run and was kept. No product worktree commits/pushes, GitHub calls or real credentials; synthetic credentials only."
